  "question": {
    "text": "<div>\r<p><span>Which of the following reactions and facts of <math> <mtext>D</mtext> </math>-glucose cannot be explained by its open chain structure?</span></p>\r\r<p><span>(i) Despite having the aldehyde group, glucose does not give Schiff test and <math> <mrow> <mtext>2,4-DNP</mtext></mrow> </math> test. </span></p>\r\r<p><span>(ii) Glucose does not react with sodium hydrogen sulphite to form addition product.</span></p>\r\r<p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>(iii) The pentaacetate of glucose does not react with hydroxyl amine showing the absence of free-<math> <mrow> <mtext>CHO</mtext></mrow> </math> group.</span></p>\r</div>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wIBkB",
      "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>(i)</span></p></div>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "79JWG",
      "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>(ii)</span></p></div>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2itsL",
      "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>(iii)</span></p></div>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ApWNO",
      "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>All of above </span></p></div>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>The above behaviour could not be explained by the open chain structure. Because one of the &ndash;OH groups of glucose add to the &ndash;CHO group and form a cyclic hemiacetal structure. It was found that glucose forms a six membered ring in which &ndash;OH at C-5 is involved in ring formation. This explains the absence of &ndash;CHO group.</span></p></div>",
    "image": null
  },
